{
  "name": "GynCycle",
  "description": "GynCycle is a mechanistic mathematical model of the human menstrual cycle that integrates follicular growth dynamics with systemic hormonal feedback loops. It employs a system of ordinary differential equations coupled with a stochastic Poisson process to simulate follicle recruitment, competition, and maturation across diverse physiological and clinical scenarios. The framework specifically enables the exploration of parameter sensitivities and the evaluation of exogenous stimulation protocols in reproductive medicine.",
